[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Spice V2 - Schematic Capture, Unified Device Descriptor and Interactive UI

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Version 2.0, 2026-11-20. Establishes schematic capture and interactive waveform probing as first-class surfaces of Spice V2, built in C#/.NET (Spice.Schematic and Spice.App) over the exact same Unified Device Descriptor and Canonical IR used by StarLark-cs, C#/F# scripts, and netlist parsers.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Unified descriptor and schematic-to-simulation contracts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-SCHEM-001
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Single fail-closed Unified Device Descriptor
STATEMENT: >>>
Every schematic and simulation device shall be backed by one canonical descriptor defining its stable ID, pin/terminal contract, typed parameters with SI units/defaults/domains, symbol binding, ERC rules, and Canonical IR lowering. Any device whose ID, terminal contract, parameter contract, or symbol cannot be resolved shall fail closed rather than falling back to a generic element or dropping parameters.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Validate catalog integrity across all built-in and OSDI devices; test missing pin, invalid unit, unknown parameter, and missing symbol failure modes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-SCHEM-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Schematic emission to Canonical IR
STATEMENT: >>>
The schematic document model (Spice.Schematic) shall compile hierarchical schematics directly into the immutable Canonical IR consumed by both XyceBackend and NativeCppBackend, preserving bidirectional component/net identity maps without accessing internal solver or model state.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Compile schematic fixtures (including hierarchical subsheets) to Canonical IR, run on XyceBackend and NativeCppBackend, and verify equivalence to hand-authored StarLark-cs/SPICE inputs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-API-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-SCHEM-003
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Electrical rule checks and hierarchical sheets
STATEMENT: >>>
Spice.Schematic shall support hierarchical subsheets, buses/ports, global power/ground nets, parameterized instances, and pre-simulation electrical rule checks (floating pins, shorted conflicting sources, missing ground reference, unresolved model references) with exact schematic element/coordinate diagnostics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Execute ERC test suite on valid hierarchical designs and deliberate connectivity/source-conflict/parameter-error schematics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-STATE-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-SCHEM-004
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Live cross-probing and waveform integration
STATEMENT: >>>
Spice.App shall link schematic nets, pins, and device branches deterministically to ResultManifest signal IDs for live cross-probing, DC operating-point annotations on the schematic, and synchronized waveform viewing (analog plots, Bode/Smith charts, FFT, and VCD digital traces). Display downsampling shall never alter underlying analysis data or measurements.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Verify deterministic net/pin-to-signal mapping across flattened hierarchy, live streaming updates during runs, and exact agreement between probed cursor values and exported Arrow/RAW data.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-DATA-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-API-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-SCHEM-005
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Versioned persistence and publication exports
STATEMENT: >>>
Schematic documents shall persist in a versioned, deterministic, Git-diffable file format and support clean export to canonical SPICE netlists, StarLark-cs scripts, BOMs, and vector/hardcopy graphics (SVG/PDF) derived from the same Unified Device Descriptor.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Round-trip save/load stability tests, schema-version migration/rejection tests, deterministic SVG/netlist export checks, bulk SPICE .LIB/.MOD/.SUB library importer dry-run/persistence/fail-closed diagnostics tests, and live NativeCppBackend simulation across the 34-part curated Foundation library (Spice.Tests/M1PlatformTests.cs, SliceCLibraryAndModelPacksTests.cs).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

